# SwissCivicQA-4L: does Apertus know the Swiss Constitution equally well in all four national languages?

**Track 1B: Swiss Voices · Core Task Intelligence** · Hack Apertus Online 2026

SwissCivicQA-4L is a closed-book factual QA benchmark on the Swiss Federal Constitution (SR 101). Every one of
**122 facts** is asked in **German, French, Italian and Romansh** (488 items), so we can measure not only
*whether* Apertus knows Swiss constitutional facts, but whether it knows them **consistently across the national
languages**. 20 facts are **false-premise** questions that measure whether the model invents details instead of
correcting the premise.

Every gold answer is grounded verbatim in the **official** Fedlex text of the same language; the validator
fails the build if a single evidence span does not occur in the cited article/paragraph.

| | |
|---|---|
| Model under test | `swiss-ai/Apertus-v1.5-8B` (text-only GGUF Q8_0 conversion by A. Martin, run with llama.cpp on CPU) |
| Judge | `gemma-3-12b-it` Q4_K_M (open weights, local), SimpleQA three-way grading, audited by rules and a blind human review of 20 % |
| Source | Federal Constitution, consolidated version of 3 March 2024 (in force), DE/FR/IT/RM, SHA-256 pinned |
| Licences | code Apache-2.0 · dataset CDLA-Permissive-2.0 · docs CC-BY-4.0 |

## Quick start

```bash
make run        # Docker; rebuilds the dataset, runs tests, recomputes every metric and checks it
                # against results/expected/<model>.json. No model, no GPU, no API key, < 1 min.
make full       # Optional: downloads both GGUF models (SHA-256 checked), starts llama.cpp servers via
                # docker-compose.full.yml and re-runs inference + judging from scratch (CPU, a few hours).
```

Evaluate another model: start any OpenAI-compatible server and run
`MODEL_URL=http://host:port/v1 JUDGE_URL=... MODEL_NAME=my-model python -m swisscivicqa.pipeline full`
(with `PYTHONPATH=src`).

## Layout

```
data/raw/            official Fedlex HTML (DE/FR/IT/RM) + SHA256SUMS
data/processed/      parsed constitution, article/paragraph JSON
data/source/         the 122 facts: questions, gold answers, evidence spans (the curated part)
data/dataset/        eval.jsonl (test cases) and metadata.jsonl (provenance + licence per item)
data/results/        model responses and judgments (JSONL)
data/human_review/   blind human labels for the 20 % audit sample
src/swisscivicqa/    parse · validate · build · infer · grade · score · review · pipeline
tests/               unit tests (grading rules, metrics, parser, dataset integrity)
docs/                challenge description, annotator consent form
```

## AI assistance

Questions, translations and code were drafted with the help of an AI assistant (Claude, Anthropic). Correctness of
every gold answer is enforced mechanically (verbatim evidence span in the official text of the same language), and
the grading was audited by a blind human review. See the technical report for details.
